<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.berwilson.cron-job-runner</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>curl -sS -m 3500 -H "Authorization: Bearer $(grep '^CRON_SECRET=' /Users/richardwhite/berwilson-platform/.env.local | cut -d= -f2-)" http://localhost:3000/api/cron/job-runner</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    Every minute: take the next queued job from /jobs and run it.

    ⚠ `-m 3500` AND NOT THE USUAL 280. Every other agent here asks a question
    that answers in seconds; a job is open-ended work and its own wall-clock
    budget (JOB_TIME_BUDGET_MS, one hour) is what brings it in to land. A curl
    that gave up at 280s would abort the request mid-job.

    ⚠ StartInterval AND NOT StartCalendarInterval, because launchd will not run
    a second copy of a job that is still running — so the one-minute tick is
    self-limiting and needs no lock of its own. `claimNextJob` refuses a second
    concurrent job anyway, for the harder reason: LM Studio serves ONE request
    at a time, so two jobs would only interleave in the same queue.

    ⚠ THIS IS THE GUARANTEE, NOT THE TRIGGER. Creating a job kicks the runner
    directly so the normal wait is seconds. What this agent is for is the case
    that kick cannot cover: the app restarting mid-job. `npm run build` IS the
    deploy and a kickstart kills in-flight work (§12), so a job checkpoints
    after every round and a `working` row whose heartbeat has gone quiet is
    reclaimed here on the next tick.

    ⚠ IT STANDS ASIDE FOR A LIVE BER AI QUESTION (interactiveRunInFlight) —
    the clearest case of any pass, since a job is work somebody handed over and
    /intel is somebody sitting there waiting. `?force=1` overrides.
  -->
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>60</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/richardwhite/Library/Logs/berwilson/cron-job-runner.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/richardwhite/Library/Logs/berwilson/cron-job-runner.log</string>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
